initial_prompt was used instead of WhisperX hotwords: faster-whisper's get_prompt places hotwords in the same sot_prev slot as the previous-text prompt, so passing both would only duplicate the terms, and initial_prompt is the one option the mlx backend also supports. video_context was left out of the prompt on purpose: it is usually written in English, and a prompt in another language than the speech can push Whisper towards transcribing (or translating) into that language. Terms are joined with 、 and end in 。 for CJK so the prompt reads as Japanese/Chinese text; on the sample video this also brought back punctuation in a stretch Whisper had returned unpunctuated, which helps segmentation (#29). The glossary dict is loaded once in main and stored as config['GLOSSARY'] so its content enters the stage fingerprints; fingerprinting GLOSSARY_FILE (a path) meant editing the file never re-ran translate either.
